      <documentation>This view provides a comprehensive list of systems engineering life cycle processes, and is intended to serve as a guide for practitioners working in the field of systems engineering. By consulting this view, users can gain a better understanding of the various processes involved in systems engineering, and how they fit together to form a cohesive whole. This knowledge can be invaluable in helping to ensure the successful development and implementation of complex systems.&#xD;
&#xD;
Created on: 27.06.2019&#xD;
Updated on: 28.03.2022, v.2.0&#xD;
&#xD;
Source and Copyright:&#xD;
This product contains quotations from the Book &quot;INCOSE Systems Engineering Handbook: A Guide for System Life Cycle Processes and Activities, 4th Edition&quot;, ISBN: 978-1-118-99940-0, published by  John Wiley &amp; Sons, Inc., authored by David D. Walden, ESEP, Garry J. Roedler, ESEP, Kevin J. Forsberg, ESEP, R. Douglas Hamelin, Thomas M. Shortell, CSEP. Permission is granted by John Wiley &amp; Sons, Inc. All rights reserved.&#xD;
</documentation>
      <property key="de_Name" value="01 - Systemlebenszyklusprozesse"/>
      <property key="en_Name" value="01 - System Life-Cycle Processes"/>
      <property key="de_Desc" value="Diese Ansicht enthält die Liste der Systems Engineering Lebenszyklus-Prozesse&#xD;&#xA;Erstellt am: 27.06.2019&#xD;&#xA;Aktualisiert am: 30.10.2020, v.1.0&#xD;&#xA;Das Produkt der GfSE (German INCOSE Chapter): prozessmodell.gfse.de"/>
      <property key="en_Desc" value="This view provides a comprehensive list of systems engineering life cycle processes, and is intended to serve as a guide for practitioners working in the field of systems engineering. By consulting this view, users can gain a better understanding of the various processes involved in systems engineering, and how they fit together to form a cohesive whole. This knowledge can be invaluable in helping to ensure the successful development and implementation of complex systems.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Created on: 27.06.2019&#xD;&#xA;Updated on: 28.03.2022, v.2.0&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Source and Copyright:&#xD;&#xA;This product contains quotations from the Book &quot;INCOSE Systems Engineering Handbook: A Guide for System Life Cycle Processes and Activities, 4th Edition&quot;, ISBN: 978-1-118-99940-0, published by  John Wiley &amp; Sons, Inc., authored by David D. Walden, ESEP, Garry J. Roedler, ESEP, Kevin J. Forsberg, ESEP, R. Douglas Hamelin, Thomas M. Shortell, CSEP. Permission is granted by John Wiley &amp; Sons, Inc. All rights reserved.&#xD;&#xA;"/>
